@startuml
title Impersonate User

actor Administrator as Admin
boundary "Admin Users Page" as UI
control "AdminUserController" as Controller
control "UserManagementService" as Service
collections "Session Store" as SessionStore
control "Auth Facade" as Auth
control "Logger" as Logger

Admin -> UI : click Impersonate on target user
UI -> Controller : POST /admin/users/{user}/impersonate
activate Controller

note over Controller
Admin middleware already guarantees an authenticated
and authorized administrator before this action runs.
end note

Controller -> Service : startImpersonation(targetUser, admin)
activate Service

note over Service
Business rules enforced here:
- administrator cannot impersonate self
- admin accounts cannot be impersonated
- original admin id is stored in session
end note

Service -> Service : validateImpersonationRules(targetUser, admin)

alt targetUser is the current administrator
    Service --> Controller : DomainException("You cannot impersonate yourself")
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> UI : 422 / error message
    deactivate Controller
    UI --> Admin : show rejection
else targetUser has admin role
    Service --> Controller : DomainException("Admin accounts cannot be impersonated")
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> UI : 422 / error message
    deactivate Controller
    UI --> Admin : show rejection
else targetUser is eligible
    Service -> SessionStore : put("impersonator_id", admin.id)
    activate SessionStore
    SessionStore --> Service : stored
    deactivate SessionStore

    Service -> Auth : login(targetUser)
    activate Auth
    Auth --> Service : authenticated as target user
    deactivate Auth

    Service -> Logger : info("Impersonation started")
    Logger --> Service : logged

    Service --> Controller : impersonation started
    deactivate Service
    Controller --> UI : 302 redirect dashboard + flash info
    deactivate Controller
    UI --> Admin : dashboard shown as target user
end

note over Service
The stop-impersonation flow restores the original
administrator using session key impersonator_id.
end note

@enduml